WEBVTT

01:50.260 --> 01:53.190
[TITAN 29A laughing]

02:00.470 --> 02:02.870
[NANABA] Rookies!
Stay where you are!

02:02.900 --> 02:05.200
We've got this.

02:05.240 --> 02:08.170
Let the ODM gear do
what it was designed for.

02:10.410 --> 02:13.080
Attack!

02:28.460 --> 02:30.730
[HENNING] Someone was here
not that long ago.

02:30.760 --> 02:33.130
[NANABA] A place
this close to the wall?

02:33.170 --> 02:36.000
[LYNNE] Bandits probably
used it as a hideout.

02:36.070 --> 02:39.600
[NANABA] A sign on the way in
said "Ruins of Utgard Castle."

02:39.640 --> 02:43.140
I didn't know there was a
historical site around here.

02:44.180 --> 02:46.980
Hey, take a look at
what I just stumbled on.

02:47.010 --> 02:49.210
You're kidding!
Is that what I think it is?

02:49.250 --> 02:50.850
Uh-huh.

02:50.920 --> 02:52.920
Can't really
read the label, though.

02:52.990 --> 02:54.890
[LYNNE] You're not
gonna drink it now?

02:54.920 --> 02:56.190
[Gasps]

02:56.260 --> 02:59.520
Don't be smart.
I'm gonna save it for later.

03:00.530 --> 03:02.430
You know, there are
worse ways to spend a night

03:02.460 --> 03:05.300
than having access
to top-shelf contraband.

03:05.330 --> 03:06.630
[NANABA] Careful.
You're starting to

03:06.670 --> 03:08.470
sound like an outlaw.

03:08.500 --> 03:10.200
[Chuckles]

03:10.270 --> 03:12.600
[GELGAR] I want you kids
to try and get some rest.

03:12.640 --> 03:14.440
There shouldn't be
any Titans crawling around

03:14.470 --> 03:18.640
at this time of night, but we'll
take turns keeping watch.

03:18.680 --> 03:22.180
[GELGAR] Be ready to leave
four hours shy of daybreak.

03:22.210 --> 03:24.820
'Scuse me.
What if it turns out

03:24.850 --> 03:27.450
that Wall Rose isn't
actually compromised?

03:27.490 --> 03:29.320
Where do, uh--

03:29.350 --> 03:33.560
Where else could they
be coming from?

03:33.630 --> 03:36.360
It's our job to find out.

03:36.400 --> 03:38.760
Starting tomorrow.

03:41.470 --> 03:44.900
I'm just saying. The
situation isn't good, sure.

03:44.970 --> 03:48.870
But is it as bad as we think?

03:48.910 --> 03:51.840
You never know, right?
That's all.

03:51.880 --> 03:53.210
She's right.

03:53.250 --> 03:55.580
We haven't really
seen that many Titans.

03:55.650 --> 03:58.680
I mean, for them to have busted
through the wall, anyway.

03:58.720 --> 04:00.650
[NANABA] Only with
the initial sighting,

04:00.690 --> 04:03.350
a relatively modest handful.

04:05.860 --> 04:08.260
[YMIR] Conny?
What about your village?

04:08.330 --> 04:10.230
Totally destroyed.

04:10.260 --> 04:14.900
It was crushed to tinder
and bits of rubble.

04:14.930 --> 04:16.830
I'm, uh-- I'm sorry.

04:16.870 --> 04:19.100
Nobody got devoured, though.

04:19.170 --> 04:21.170
Looked like they all got out,

04:21.210 --> 04:24.070
so there's a silver
lining, at least.

04:24.110 --> 04:26.710
I thought that you said
it was destroyed?

04:26.750 --> 04:28.680
Well, the houses
and stuff were,

04:28.710 --> 04:31.380
but the people themselves
must've all escaped.

04:31.420 --> 04:32.850
I mean, they had to've.

04:32.890 --> 04:37.050
The thing is... we didn't
see any blood anywhere.

04:37.090 --> 04:39.120
Not so much as one drop.

04:39.190 --> 04:41.420
That's the only
possible explanation.

04:41.460 --> 04:43.860
[exhales]

04:43.900 --> 04:48.030
Still, though. Something
I can't get out of my head.

04:48.070 --> 04:51.430
There was a Titan
on top of our house.

04:51.470 --> 04:54.370
Just lying there.
Staring at me.

04:54.410 --> 04:57.540
It couldn't move
on its own, thank god.

04:57.580 --> 05:01.650
But, I just--
I have no idea why,

05:01.710 --> 05:04.480
but it reminded me
of my mom.

05:04.550 --> 05:05.880
Am I crazy?

05:05.920 --> 05:08.390
Conny. What did I tell you?

05:08.420 --> 05:10.950
--It was your imagination--
--[YMIR] Are you for real?

05:10.990 --> 05:12.660
[Laughs]

05:12.720 --> 05:15.230
You actually think
your mom might be a Titan?

05:15.260 --> 05:18.300
Oh, honey! As itty-bitty
as you are? Please!

05:18.330 --> 05:21.300
We all knew you were dumb
as a bag of rocks, but this?

05:21.330 --> 05:25.000
Whoa, man! This takes it
to whole other level!

05:25.070 --> 05:26.600
[Laughs]

05:26.640 --> 05:28.410
Ha-ha. Yeah. Have your fun.

05:28.440 --> 05:30.470
Guess I was
kinda asking for it.

05:30.510 --> 05:32.640
Don't stop there:
If Mother-darling's a Titan,

05:32.680 --> 05:35.480
it's only logical to assume
dear ol' Daddy is, too.

05:35.510 --> 05:38.850
Basic biology.
Think about it. How else--

05:38.920 --> 05:42.620
Okay, I get it!
Shut up and go to sleep!

05:51.130 --> 05:52.260
[Door clicks and creaks]

05:52.300 --> 05:54.260
[REINER]
Ymir? What are you doing?

05:54.330 --> 05:57.670
Heh. Seriously?
What're you doing?

05:57.740 --> 05:59.100
Here to ravage me?

05:59.140 --> 06:00.470
Don't take this wrong way,

06:00.510 --> 06:02.840
but I didn't think you were
all that into girls.

06:02.870 --> 06:05.210
Really? Well, since
we're on the subject,

06:05.280 --> 06:08.010
I didn't think you were
all that into guys.

06:08.050 --> 06:11.450
Heh. If you must know
I'm scavenging for leftovers

06:11.480 --> 06:13.520
like a street urchin.

06:13.550 --> 06:16.650
I'd prefer not to meet my
maker on an empty stomach.

06:16.690 --> 06:18.520
[Door creaks]

06:18.560 --> 06:21.490
[REINER] Look, the whole thing
earlier with Conny.

06:21.530 --> 06:25.460
Were you teasing him to
get his mind off of things?

06:25.500 --> 06:28.000
It'd be great if you
could keep that up.

06:28.030 --> 06:32.070
The less he dwells on his
family right now, the better.

06:32.140 --> 06:33.870
What are you talking about?

06:33.910 --> 06:36.210
Huh. This might be good.

06:36.240 --> 06:39.040
Herring's not my favorite,
but whatever.

06:39.080 --> 06:43.810
[REINER]
Herring, huh? Can I see?

06:43.850 --> 06:46.250
Help yourself.

06:46.320 --> 06:48.690
I can't believe
there's canned food here.

06:48.720 --> 06:50.820
[Gasps]

06:50.860 --> 06:53.990
What, the--
Wait, what is this?

06:54.030 --> 06:56.730
I can't read a word of it.

06:56.800 --> 06:59.860
How do you know
this says "herring?"

07:00.930 --> 07:08.070
This, uh, label.
It's in another language.

07:08.170 --> 07:11.110
Ymir. How can you--?

07:13.410 --> 07:14.710
Everyone, wake up!

07:14.750 --> 07:17.350
Get to the tower immediately!

07:20.750 --> 07:22.520
[GELGAR]
Bother someone else.

07:22.550 --> 07:24.590
I should be drinking
right now, damn it!

07:24.620 --> 07:27.890
You're standing between me
and a tankard of ale!

07:29.700 --> 07:32.260
[NANABA]
Attack!

07:35.970 --> 07:37.800
Think it's gonna
be that easy, big guy?

07:37.870 --> 07:40.840
I got news for ya! Aah!

07:43.540 --> 07:46.680
[NANABA yells]

07:51.650 --> 07:52.980
[GELGAR]
Hot damn!

07:53.050 --> 07:55.750
You little ones should watch
where you're going! Heh!

07:55.790 --> 07:57.590
Dumb-asses.

07:57.620 --> 07:59.220
I don't think
you're one to talk.

07:59.260 --> 08:00.960
There's no call
to be so reckless.

08:00.990 --> 08:02.930
Did you have to
waste your blades?

08:02.960 --> 08:05.260
That's just how I do things.

08:05.300 --> 08:07.400
You'd better chalk
that one up as an assist.

08:07.430 --> 08:11.800
Aren't you the hero.
I'll think about it.

08:14.440 --> 08:16.210
[Grunts]

08:18.180 --> 08:22.250
[LYNNE]
Oh, no. I'm too late.

08:22.280 --> 08:24.580
The door's
been kicked down!

08:25.450 --> 08:26.750
Titans are in the castle!

08:26.790 --> 08:29.320
Get below and improvise
some sort a barricade!

08:29.390 --> 08:33.790
Be careful. Retreat back up
here only as a last resort!

08:33.830 --> 08:35.760
Now hurry. The rest of us
will keep any more

08:35.790 --> 08:39.300
from getting in as best we can.

08:39.330 --> 08:43.170
There are quite a few.
So this might be it for us.

08:43.200 --> 08:45.870
But by god we'll fight
to the last breath.

08:45.940 --> 08:49.670
Our heart and soul to
the cause, right? Now go!

08:49.710 --> 08:51.340
[ALL]
Got it!

08:53.650 --> 08:56.110
I'll go see how far
they've gotten in.

08:56.150 --> 08:58.480
You find something
to board up the entrance!

08:58.520 --> 09:00.380
Whatever isn't nailed down!

09:00.450 --> 09:01.480
Reiner, wait!

09:01.520 --> 09:02.820
What the hell?

09:02.850 --> 09:05.320
Hang on, we're coming!
Wait up!

09:05.390 --> 09:06.690
Are you kidding me?

09:06.730 --> 09:09.160
Why's he always gotta be
the first one to step up?

09:09.190 --> 09:10.660
Give us a break!

09:10.700 --> 09:13.600
I know. It's a habit of his.

09:24.040 --> 09:26.710
[REINER]
Are they in the tower?

09:28.180 --> 09:29.880
The door's still barred.

09:29.980 --> 09:32.820
Not that that'll
keep 'em out for long.

09:47.330 --> 09:50.370
[growls lowly]

09:50.400 --> 09:53.240
[REINER groans]

09:53.270 --> 09:55.100
They're in the tower!

09:55.170 --> 09:57.570
Get down here and help me!

09:57.610 --> 09:59.510
[TITAN 29C growls]

10:01.880 --> 10:05.920
[REINER] Is this it?
Is this how I go out?

10:05.950 --> 10:08.280
Son of a bitch!

10:22.430 --> 10:27.200
[REINER]
No. Not yet.

10:27.240 --> 10:29.240
I refuse!

10:32.980 --> 10:35.380
[REINER]
I'm going back home!

10:35.410 --> 10:37.050
[BERTHOLDT]
Reiner!

10:39.150 --> 10:40.480
[Yells]

10:40.550 --> 10:44.120
[TITAN 29C groans]

10:44.160 --> 10:45.890
Talk to me, man.
Are you good?

10:45.920 --> 10:48.060
Yes! Listen to me.

10:48.090 --> 10:50.460
We're gonna make it home!

10:50.500 --> 10:53.000
This is not how we die!

10:53.060 --> 10:56.970
Yeah, I know. Damn right!

10:57.000 --> 10:59.500
Guys! Heads up! Incoming!

10:59.570 --> 11:02.470
Where'd you find--?
Good work! Is there ammo?

11:02.510 --> 11:03.740
Yeah, right, if only!

11:03.780 --> 11:05.510
It was pure luck
that we found this.

11:05.580 --> 11:07.810
Get out of the way!

11:25.260 --> 11:28.330
[YMIR] May miracles
never cease. Huzzah.

11:28.370 --> 11:31.200
[REINER] Yeah. It's not
getting up from that.

11:31.270 --> 11:32.870
Good thing it was a little one.

11:32.940 --> 11:35.610
What now? A knife's
the only thing we got.

11:35.640 --> 11:36.940
Should I cut the nape, or--?

11:36.980 --> 11:40.640
Don't risk it. Get grabbed,
you'll get hurt.

11:40.680 --> 11:41.780
[CHRISTA] Then, I think
it would be best

11:41.810 --> 11:45.010
if we head back
upstairs for now.

11:45.050 --> 11:46.380
We have no way
of knowing if that's

11:46.450 --> 11:48.990
the only one who got in.

11:56.820 --> 11:57.990
Huh?

11:58.060 --> 11:59.520
[CHRISTA]
Conny!

12:01.230 --> 12:02.390
Huh?

12:02.460 --> 12:03.960
[CHRISTA]
Conny!

12:09.900 --> 12:10.670
[REINER yells]

12:10.700 --> 12:12.170
Reiner, no!

12:12.240 --> 12:14.240
[Gaspss]

12:20.580 --> 12:25.380
[REINER grunts, groans]

12:25.450 --> 12:28.420
Holy-- What're you doing?

12:28.490 --> 12:30.820
Wait. Are you?

12:30.860 --> 12:33.220
Are you gonna jump out
the window with it?

12:33.260 --> 12:35.190
We've got no other choice.

12:35.230 --> 12:38.330
No! Wait!
Just give me a second!

12:38.360 --> 12:41.730
I think I can
slice its jaw open!

12:41.770 --> 12:43.800
--[CONNY] There!
--[REINER groans]

12:49.210 --> 12:50.980
[All gasp]

13:00.620 --> 13:03.090
[CONNY] What do we do
if another one gets in?

13:03.120 --> 13:06.290
Not like we'll find another
cannon lying around, am I right?

13:06.360 --> 13:09.690
Probably. Lightning
won't strike twice.

13:13.700 --> 13:16.630
--[grunts]
--Sorry, I know it stings.

13:16.700 --> 13:18.940
Plus, the bone's
most likely fractured.

13:18.970 --> 13:21.640
Of course. It's about
how my luck runs.

13:21.710 --> 13:26.010
We'll need a splint
and a bandage. Easy enough.

13:29.150 --> 13:30.680
[REINER gasps]

13:30.720 --> 13:32.480
[Cloth tearing]

13:32.550 --> 13:35.750
[CHRISTA]
The cloth's filthy.

13:35.790 --> 13:40.920
I haven't been able to wash
it in forever. I'm sorry.

13:40.960 --> 13:43.930
No sweat. It does the job.

13:43.960 --> 13:45.560
[REINER]
Marry me.

13:45.600 --> 13:47.460
So you gonna
be all right or what?

13:47.500 --> 13:50.370
Think so. Probably.

13:50.940 --> 13:52.800
Y'know, Christa, I, uh--

13:52.840 --> 13:54.910
I got a little
scratched up myself.

13:54.940 --> 13:58.840
Ugh. So just
spit on it or somethin'.

13:58.910 --> 14:02.450
Anyway, sorry about
all that, man.

14:02.480 --> 14:05.320
Seems like you're always
having to save my ass.

14:05.350 --> 14:07.280
You and everyone else.

14:07.320 --> 14:10.090
Even Annie put herself
on the line for me once.

14:10.120 --> 14:12.090
I owe you. A lot.

14:12.120 --> 14:15.790
No, no. It's fine.

14:15.830 --> 14:17.960
We have each other's back.

14:18.000 --> 14:20.700
It's what soldiers do.

14:20.770 --> 14:22.170
I don't know.

14:22.200 --> 14:24.840
I doubt I could ever
be that courageous.

14:24.870 --> 14:26.800
Has he always been like this?

14:26.840 --> 14:29.810
The self-sacrificing type?

14:29.840 --> 14:33.180
No. He's changed a bit.

14:33.210 --> 14:38.650
In the old days, Reiner
was more of a warrior.

14:38.680 --> 14:43.190
Warrior? I'm not
quite sure I understand.

14:43.660 --> 14:47.360
[YMIR] Anyway, let's scrounge
around for stuff we can use.

14:47.390 --> 14:48.830
If I have to die,
I'd rather not do it

14:48.860 --> 14:51.200
'cause we're being half-assed.

14:51.230 --> 14:54.130
Oh, wow.
Well, all right then.

14:54.170 --> 14:57.300
Say what you will,
the Scouts get shit done.

14:59.540 --> 15:01.840
[NANABA grunts]

15:01.870 --> 15:03.870
[Yells]

15:07.480 --> 15:09.510
[GELGAR] That's mostly it
for the big ones.

15:09.550 --> 15:11.420
Good thing
we have this tower.

15:11.480 --> 15:15.020
No kidding. Think we might
just survive the night.

15:15.050 --> 15:16.390
We'll check on the recruits.

15:16.460 --> 15:18.120
Okay.

15:20.490 --> 15:24.230
What the hell's that noise?

15:24.260 --> 15:26.330
[BOTH gasp]

15:26.370 --> 15:27.930
[NANABA]
The horses!

15:28.000 --> 15:30.730
[BOTH gasp]

15:30.770 --> 15:32.000
There it is again!

15:32.040 --> 15:33.900
Wha-- Where's it coming from?

15:35.210 --> 15:37.070
--[Rumble]
--[BOTH gasp]

15:39.680 --> 15:42.180
[NANABA]
Lynne! Henning!

15:47.420 --> 15:49.890
Oh shit!

15:49.920 --> 15:54.290
[GELGAR] They're dead.
Died instantly.

15:54.360 --> 15:56.430
This can't...

15:56.460 --> 15:57.690
[Gasps]
He did this!

15:57.730 --> 16:00.300
The one that made
a B-line for the wall!

16:00.370 --> 16:02.370
Hairy son of
a bitch is randomly--

16:02.400 --> 16:04.130
[Gasps]

16:04.200 --> 16:05.400
Heads up, guys!

16:05.440 --> 16:07.400
We've got twice
as many as before!

16:07.440 --> 16:08.640
You're kidding!

16:08.710 --> 16:10.010
It's like they're
timing these attacks

16:10.040 --> 16:12.710
as some part of
a larger strategy.

16:12.750 --> 16:14.710
This isn't random at all.

16:14.750 --> 16:17.180
We're being toyed with.

16:17.250 --> 16:24.920
[BEAST TITAN roars]

16:26.260 --> 16:28.230
[ALL gasp]

16:40.110 --> 16:42.070
[Grunts]

16:44.980 --> 16:48.080
[NANABA] Damn it.
I'm running out of gas!

16:53.550 --> 16:55.120
Come on, go down!

16:55.150 --> 16:57.190
[Gasps]

17:04.200 --> 17:06.760
[GELGAR]
Tower's not gonna hold.

17:06.800 --> 17:10.500
Hey, my ODM gear's
low on juice. Yours?

17:10.540 --> 17:14.170
Fresh out. And I've worn
my blades down to the nub.

17:14.270 --> 17:17.770
Please tell me those aren't
the only ones you've got left.

17:17.810 --> 17:19.440
'Fraid so.

17:19.480 --> 17:22.350
[GELGAR] How many dead Titans
the four of us rack up?

17:22.380 --> 17:23.780
[NANABA]
Couldn't say.

17:23.820 --> 17:26.550
I was too preoccupied
to keep count.

17:26.620 --> 17:30.190
[GELGAR] Yeah, well. I'm
thinkin' I didn't do too bad.

17:30.220 --> 17:33.620
Heh. Oh, man.

17:33.660 --> 17:36.930
What's a guy gotta do
to get a drink around here?

17:36.960 --> 17:39.530
This isn't the time for--
[Gasps]

17:39.570 --> 17:42.630
I'm sorry, Nanaba.

17:42.670 --> 17:44.840
I must've bashed my head.

17:44.870 --> 17:50.240
I... I don't think...
I can... hang on.

17:50.310 --> 17:52.110
[NANABA]
Gelgar!

17:56.120 --> 17:58.350
[Yell]

18:03.890 --> 18:06.320
Gelgar, no!

18:06.360 --> 18:10.130
That's it. That's
everything I've got.

18:10.160 --> 18:12.300
[Gasps]

18:16.240 --> 18:19.200
[GELGAR gasps and coughs]

18:19.240 --> 18:23.610
[Breathe laboringly]

18:23.680 --> 18:25.410
[Gasps]

18:25.440 --> 18:28.410
There is a god.

18:45.730 --> 18:48.400
Oh, come on.
This isn't fair.

18:48.430 --> 18:50.470
Why would you do me that way?

18:50.540 --> 18:52.400
[Groans]

18:52.440 --> 18:55.110
Who drank my goddamn booze?

18:55.170 --> 18:57.010
[Bottle breaks]

19:01.250 --> 19:02.910
[CONNY]
They got him.

19:04.080 --> 19:05.580
Christa, what're
you doing? Stop!

19:05.620 --> 19:07.380
The tower's
gonna give any second!

19:07.420 --> 19:08.790
You have to stay still!

19:08.820 --> 19:11.720
Let go! They're dying
in our place!

19:11.760 --> 19:14.160
--[CHRISTA] Nanaba. Gelgar.
--[NANABA] No! No! Stop it!

19:14.230 --> 19:15.930
Please! I'm sorry, Daddy!

19:15.960 --> 19:19.200
I'll be a good girl
from now on, I promise!

19:19.230 --> 19:21.430
No, Daddy! No--!

19:21.470 --> 19:23.100
--[Squelch]
--[BOTH gasp]

19:23.140 --> 19:26.770
Aah! Goddamn it! Now what?

19:26.810 --> 19:28.640
We sit around waiting
for the tower to collapse

19:28.670 --> 19:31.310
and let ourselves
get eaten alive?

19:31.380 --> 19:35.010
That's it? There's nothing
else we can do?

19:35.080 --> 19:37.110
This is bullshit.
We'll be wiped out

19:37.150 --> 19:39.820
before getting to finish
what we started.

19:39.920 --> 19:42.650
[Grunts]

19:42.690 --> 19:45.160
No, this--
This isn't over yet.

19:45.190 --> 19:47.790
If I could find a weapon,
I'd go down fighting.

19:47.830 --> 19:50.660
At least try to be worthy of
the people who died for us.

19:50.700 --> 19:52.200
Christa, please.
Enough with that

19:52.260 --> 19:55.030
kinda crap already, okay?

19:55.100 --> 19:57.100
Don't use their deaths
as an excuse.

19:57.140 --> 19:58.770
They didn't sacrifice
themselves so you could

19:58.800 --> 20:01.970
fulfill some fantasy about
going out in a blaze of glory.

20:02.010 --> 20:04.140
[CHRISTA gasps]
Ymir! You know

20:04.180 --> 20:05.540
that's not what I meant!

20:05.610 --> 20:07.280
And you damn-well know
you're not like Conny

20:07.310 --> 20:09.210
and the others!

20:09.280 --> 20:12.080
They're in this to give
humanity a fighting chance.

20:12.120 --> 20:13.450
Deep down all you care about

20:13.490 --> 20:16.650
is having the word "hero"
carved on your epitaph.

20:16.690 --> 20:19.020
That-- That's not it at all.

20:19.060 --> 20:22.060
[YMIR] Conny. Where's
that knife you had?

20:22.130 --> 20:24.460
[CONNY]
Huh? Why?

20:24.500 --> 20:26.160
[YMIR]
Just give it here.

20:26.200 --> 20:28.970
Fine. Whatever.

20:30.840 --> 20:32.670
You're very sweet, thanks.

20:32.700 --> 20:34.870
[CONNY] What do you
even need it for?

20:34.910 --> 20:39.380
Hm. Not much. I'm, uh--

20:39.410 --> 20:42.080
Just gonna
give 'em a little hell.

20:42.150 --> 20:45.020
Okay, then.
So, do you have a plan?

20:45.050 --> 20:49.150
If I do, we'll learn
what it is together.

20:49.190 --> 20:51.820
Ymir.

20:51.860 --> 20:55.230
[YMIR]
Christa. Listen to me.

20:55.260 --> 20:57.430
I realize you've
probably forgotten.

20:57.500 --> 21:02.430
[Rumble]

21:02.500 --> 21:07.040
But, since we're facing
the end, try to think back.

21:07.070 --> 21:10.540
Remember that oath that we
made on the snowy mountain.

21:12.880 --> 21:15.710
I have no business telling
you how to live your life.

21:15.750 --> 21:18.220
It's not my place.

21:18.250 --> 21:20.520
So, I guess
when you break it down,

21:20.550 --> 21:24.120
this is really
just more of a hope.

21:24.190 --> 21:28.390
Christa. Live a life
you can be proud of.

21:34.800 --> 21:39.070
[Gasps]

21:39.100 --> 21:42.940
Never forget
the promise we made.

21:42.980 --> 21:44.210
Ymir, wait!

21:44.240 --> 21:45.940
--[REINER and BERTHOLDT gasp]
--[CHRISTA yells]

21:49.580 --> 21:51.950
[CHRISTA]
Ymir!

21:52.720 --> 21:54.520
[Grunts]

22:05.100 --> 22:07.860
[Yells]

22:10.300 --> 22:15.270
♪ Closing Song ♪
